16 0 obj
<< /A 65 0 R /Alt (Bar chart illustrating the class distribution in an eye diseases dataset, showing diabetic retinopathy, normal, cataract, and glaucoma classes, each with image counts ranging from about 1,000 to 1,100.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 66 0 R /Alt (Grid of sixteen fundus eye images shows four preprocessing stages for four conditions: cataract, diabetic retinopathy, glaucoma, and normal. Columns display original RGB, cropped and resized, CLAHE enhanced, and Ben-Graham normalized versions. Each row represents one eye condition.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a deep learning workflow for fundus image classification, showing parallel Swin Transformer and EfficientNet-B4 branches, QICAF fusion, bilinear entanglement fusion, classification head outputting cataract, diabetic retinopathy, glaucoma, or normal, concluding with an explainability stage.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 68 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram showing a machine learning model pipeline. Global and local tokens serve as inputs to amplitude encoding, followed by a unitary phase gate and fidelity-inspired similarity. Subsequent steps include Born-rule normalisation, attended representation, entanglement fusion, and final classification. Mathematical expressions are included for each process stage.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 69 0 R /Alt (Circuit schematic for Quantum-Inspired Cross-Attention with two input states passing through amplitude encoding, unitary phase gate, fidelity similarity calculation, quantum measurement using Born rule, and entanglement fusion, resulting in a classifier output.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 70 0 R /Alt (Triple line graph displaying model loss, accuracy, and macro-F1 score across forty-five epochs for training and validation sets. Loss decreases over epochs, while accuracy and macro-F1 scores both increase, with validation performance consistently outperforming training.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 51 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 71 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side confusion matrix plots display classification performance for four eye disease categories. The left plot shows raw counts; the right plot shows normalized percentages, highlighting strong diagonal values for cataract, diabetic retinopathy, glaucoma, and normal labels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 52 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 72 0 R /Alt (Line graph showing one-vs-rest ROC curves for test set classification of cataract, diabetic retinopathy, glaucoma, and normal conditions, with AUC values ranging from 0.991 to 1.000, all curves closely approach the top left corner indicating high model performance.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 52 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 73 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing 5-fold cross-validation results for validation macro-F1 scores using test-time augmentation. Scores by fold: Fold 0, 0.9542; Fold 1, 0.9293; Fold 2, 0.9388; Fold 3, 0.9263; Fold 4, 0.9302. Dashed line marks the mean macro-F1 score of 0.9358 with a standard deviation of 0.0113.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 53 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 74 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing Macro-F1 \(TTA\) scores of QICAF-Net and five single-backbone baselines: EfficientNet-B3 \(0.9326\), DenseNet-121 \(0.9390\), ResNet-50 \(0.9455\), ViT-Small \(0.9487\), QICAF-Net \(0.9420\), and Swin-Tiny \(0.9583\). QICAF-Net is highlighted in red.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 54 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 75 0 R /Alt (Bar chart titled \21518-run multi-seed ablation \(6 configs × 3 seeds\)\216 compares six configurations by their Macro-F1 scores \(three-seed mean\), all scoring between 0.9403 and 0.9426, with error bars representing variability.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 54 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 76 0 R /Alt (Two side-by-side confusion matrices showing external classification performance for cataract, diabetic retinopathy \(DR\), glaucoma and normal. The left matrix shows counts and the right shows row-normalised proportions. Most cataract and normal cases are correctly predicted. Diabetic retinopathy is often misclassified as cataract or glaucoma, and some glaucoma cases are predicted as normal. Darker green shading indicates higher values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 55 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
28 0 obj
<< /A 77 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing external per-class ROC-AUC and PR-AUC for Cataract, DR, Glaucoma, and Normal, showing higher ROC-AUC than PR-AUC for all except Normal where PR-AUC is highest.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 56 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
29 0 obj
<< /A 78 0 R /Alt (Four rows of images display fundus photographs, heatmaps using Grad-CAM++, and overlays for cataract, diabetic retinopathy, glaucoma, and normal eye conditions, with each overlay showing the predicted diagnosis at the bottom.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 57 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
30 0 obj
<< /A 79 0 R /Alt (Panel of twelve images in four rows depicting ocular fundus images for cataract, diabetic retinopathy, glaucoma, and normal cases. Each row contains the original fundus image, a heatmap labeled \215QICAF attention,\216 and an overlay combining the fundus and attention map, illustrating regions of algorithmic focus for each medical condition.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 58 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
31 0 obj
<< /A 80 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing normalized AUC values for deletion and insertion explanation faithfulness across four categories: cataract, diabetic retinopathy, glaucoma, and normal. Teal bars represent deletion AUC and red bars represent insertion AUC.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 59 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
32 0 obj
<< /A 81 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing the computational cost of five single-backbone models and QICAF-Net using single-view GFLOPs and no-TTA latency in milliseconds per image. QICAF-Net has the highest values for both metrics. EfficientNet-B3 has the lowest GFLOPs, and ViT-Small has the lowest latency.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 59 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
33 0 obj
<< /A 82 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing accuracy and macro-F1 scores for four experimental conditions in an external cohort of 3,907 samples. Accuracy scores are highest for Raw TTA and CC TTA at 0.873 and 0.874, while macro-F1 scores are highest for CC TTA and Raw TTA at 0.719 and 0.715. Raw no-TTA and CC no-TTA both show lower scores, with accuracy at 0.856 and macro-F1 at 0.686.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 60 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
